SUMMARY:The Integration Blueprint: Choosing the Right Path in Microsoft Fa
 bric (APAC)
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn a world of multiple tools and en
 dless data sources\, how do you design the right integration strategy in M
 icrosoft Fabric?\n\nJoin us for a **live demo-driven session** that breaks
  down the **real-world patterns\, use cases\,** and **best practices** for
  **landing\, transforming\, and orchestrating data** in Microsoft Fabric.\
 nWhether you’re working with a Lakehouse\, Data Warehouse\, Eventhouse\,
  or SQL Database\, this session gives you the playbook to select and combi
 ne the right tools for the job.\n\n**We’ll walk through:**\n• Landing 
 data using Data Pipelines\, OneLake shortcuts\, and external connections\n
 • Transforming and cleaning data using Notebooks (Spark) for scale and f
 lexibility\n• Business logic and last-mile transformation using Dataflow
 s Gen2\n• How to orchestrate it all using Fabric Data Pipelines for repe
 atable\, maintainable workflows\n• When and why to land your data into L
 akehouses\, Data Warehouses\, Eventhouses\, or SQL endpoints\n\n**You’ll
  walk away with:**\n• A clear understanding of which tools to use when a
 cross the Fabric integration stack\n• A working knowledge of how to comb
 ine multiple integration techniques in one solution\n• Architecture patt
 erns and decision criteria for building scalable data landing zones\nLive 
 demos you can replicate to accelerate your own Fabric journey\n\nJoin the 
 Fabric Data Days Monthly Sessions- https://aka.ms/fdd/monthly
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3140
 27481/
